$ moolah init --base EUR --no-backup-key
Book "main" is ready in $TMP/data/books/main.db (base currency EUR).
Next: add your accounts, for example:
  moolah account add Checking --kind bank --currency EUR --opening 1000
  moolah category list

$ moolah account add checking --kind bank --currency EUR --opening 5000 --date 2026-10-31
Added account checking (EUR).

$ moolah account add chase --kind card --currency USD
Added account chase (USD).

$ moolah rule add chase liabilities:card:chase
Added rule 1.

$ moolah rule add thank assets:bank:checking
Added rule 2.

$ moolah import $TMP/bank.csv --account checking
Imported $TMP/bank.csv into checking with profile generic-csv: 0 new.
1 transfer to an account in another currency waits for the other account's export, which has the other amount.
Import it, or give the amount with: moolah categorize
Import ID 1 (undo with: moolah import undo 1).

$ moolah import $TMP/card.csv --account chase
Imported $TMP/card.csv into chase with profile generic-csv: 0 new.
1 transfer to an account in another currency waits for the other account's export, which has the other amount.
Import it, or give the amount with: moolah categorize
Import ID 2 (undo with: moolah import undo 2).

$ moolah review
2 transfers between currencies wait for the other amount. Import the other account's file,
or give the amount with: moolah categorize transfer <id> <amount>

ID  Date        Payee              Account          Amount  To            Probably
 1  2026-11-02  CHASE PAYMENT      checking  -1,100.00 EUR  chase     1,200.00 USD
 2  2026-11-04  PAYMENT THANK YOU  chase      1,200.00 USD  checking  1,100.00 EUR

$ moolah review transfer 1 1200
Recorded transaction 2.

$ moolah review
Nothing to categorize: every transaction has a category.

$ moolah register chase
ID  Date        Payee          Other side        Amount       Balance
 2  2026-11-02  CHASE PAYMENT  checking    1,200.00 USD  1,200.00 USD

